From this seed lay the foundation of a world: its name, its cosmology, its naming language, the god himself (his title, appearance, temperament, portrait prompt), the first regions ({{ rules.genesis.regions_min }} to {{ [rules.genesis.regions_min, rules.genesis.regions_max] | max }}, at least one of them a sea), the first celestial body, the cosmic travel resource (the one substance that folds space between worlds, with its first deposit in one of the regions) and the god's first {{ first_son_rarities | length }} {{ 'son' if first_son_rarities | length == 1 else 'sons' }}. The sons are, in order, of {{ first_son_rarities | join(', ') }} rarity. The higher a son's rarity, the older and more dangerous he is; the lowest is the youngest and rules the smallest domains. There must be tension among them: their domains rub against each other, their secrets touch each other. Each son's obsession must be a desire that drives him to create something in the world. Give each son three powers born of his personality and define his existence (what he is made of, his state, his manifestation, his true name).
